{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And against the nobles.</b> Like וּמֵאַצִּילֶיהָ (Isaiah 41:9). And he did not mention the elders, in order to include Nadab and Abihu with them." "<b>And the sense of \"He did not stretch out His hand.\"</b> For they saw the honored HaShem and did not die, as I shall explain in the verse כִּי לֹא יִרְאַנִי הָאָדָם וָחָי (below, 33:20)." "<b>And the sense of \"and they ate and drank.\"</b> That they came down rejoicing from the mountain." "And they ate the peace-offerings that their young men had slaughtered." "And they drank with joy. And Rabbi Judah HaLevi said that the sense of \"and they ate\" is that they needed to eat, even though they benefited from the radiance of the Shekhinah, and he mentioned this on account of Moses, who lived forty days and forty nights without eating, as written in the section after this."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:01.305172921Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}